## Bun workspace validation

Before installation or delegated validation:

- confirm the root package name and every child package name are valid and
  unique;
- confirm `{{frontend.root}}`, `{{backend.root}}`, and
  `{{workspace.sharedPackageRoots}}` are normalized, target-relative, and
  non-overlapping;
- reject duplicate workspace entries, unresolved placeholders, and ownership
  collisions;
- confirm each materialized workspace entry contains its own `package.json`;
- use `bun install --frozen-lockfile` when a committed `bun.lock` already
  exists, then invoke only the package-local checks relevant to the change.

Absence of a frontend or backend structure provider is not itself a failure.
The configured paths must still be coherent and remain owned by whichever
later piece creates them.
